    "title": "pandas.DatetimeIndex.quarter — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DatetimeIndex.quarter#\n\n- property DatetimeIndex.quarter[source]#\n- The quarter of the date. See also \n  - `DatetimeIndex.snap`\n  - Snap time stamps to nearest occurring frequency.\n  - `DatetimeIndex.time`\n  - Returns numpy array of datetime.time objects. The time part of the Timestamps.\n Examples For Series: >>> s = pd.Series([\"1/1/2020 10:00:00+00:00\", \"4/1/2020 11:00:00+00:00\"]) >>> s = pd.to_datetime(s) >>> s 0 2020-01-01 10:00:00+00:00 1 2020-04-01 11:00:00+00:00 dtype: datetime64[us, UTC] >>> s.dt.quarter 0 1 1 2 dtype: int32 For DatetimeIndex: >>> idx = pd.DatetimeIndex([\"1/1/2020 10:00:00+00:00\", ... \"2/1/2020 11:00:00+00:00\"]) >>> idx.quarter Index([1, 1], dtype='int32')",
    "markdown_length": 697,
